config BOARD_BANGLE2
    bool
    default y

config BANGLE2_TEST_NO_WDT_STARTUP_FEED
    bool "TEST ONLY: skip the startup HW-watchdog feeds (Renode honesty RED test)"
    default n
    help
      When set, main() does NOT issue the early watchdog_feed() before
      rtc_init(), and the RTC COMPARE_1 interrupt does NOT call
      task_watchdog_startup_feed(). This produces a dedicated RED-test ELF
      that MUST fail the Renode early-RR0-feed honesty check: with the
      startup feeds removed, no CPU write reaches NRF_WDT->RR[0] in the
      early boot window. Never enable in a shipping build.

config WATCHDOG_SELF_ARM
    bool
    default y if BOARD_BANGLE2
    help
      Bare-metal full-flash boards have no bootloader to arm the hardware
      watchdog. When set, main() arms the driver's own WDT (nrf5.c: 8 s,
      RR0) early in boot, immediately before rtc_init.

config BANGLE2_TEST_NO_WDT_ARM
    bool "TEST ONLY: skip the boot-time WDT self-arm (Renode honesty RED test)"
    default n
    help
      When set, main() does NOT call watchdog_init()/watchdog_start(), so
      the hardware watchdog is never armed. This produces a dedicated
      RED-test ELF that MUST fail the Renode wdt_arm honesty check: no CPU
      write reaches NRF_WDT->TASKS_START and RUNSTATUS stays 0 after boot.
      Never enable in a shipping build.
